        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Damage Mechanics and NDT Inspection",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   LOW-VELOCITY IMPACT (< 10 m/s):\n   ─────────────────────────────────\n   Source: tools dropped during maintenance, runway debris, hail\n   Typical mass × velocity: 1 kg × 5 m/s, 2.3 kg × 6 m/s (FAA requirement)"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-DAMAGE-INSPECTION.md#007",
      "path": [
        "08-DAMAGE-INSPECTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:composite-materials:08-damage-inspection, git-history:composite-materials:08-damage-inspection]",
        "canonical_path": "composite-materials/08-DAMAGE-INSPECTION.md",
        "concepts": "[damage, inspection]",
        "current_path": "composite-materials/08-DAMAGE-INSPECTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:composite-materials:damage-inspection",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "composite-materials",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[damage, inspection]",
        "section": "composite-materials",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Damage Mechanics and NDT Inspection",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DAMAGE SEQUENCE:\n   ──────────────────\n   Initial contact: compressive through-thickness stress cone\n   → Matrix cracks propagate radially from impact point\n   → Delaminations grow at ply interfaces (driven by interlaminar shear)\n   → Conical delamination pattern (each ply interface, growing with depth)\n   → Fiber fracture at back face (tension) when contact force high"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-DAMAGE-INSPECTION.md#008",
      "path": [
        "08-DAMAGE-INSPECTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:composite-materials:08-damage-inspection, git-history:composite-materials:08-damage-inspection]",
        "canonical_path": "composite-materials/08-DAMAGE-INSPECTION.md",
        "concepts": "[damage, inspection]",
        "current_path": "composite-materials/08-DAMAGE-INSPECTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:composite-materials:damage-inspection",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "composite-materials",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[damage, inspection]",
        "section": "composite-materials",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Damage Mechanics and NDT Inspection",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SURFACE APPEARANCE:\n   ────────────────────\n   Small dent (0.1–3 mm depth for BVID threshold)\n   Subsurface: large delamination (~3–10× projected surface damage area)\n   \"Iceberg effect\": most damage invisible from surface"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-DAMAGE-INSPECTION.md#009",
      "path": [
        "08-DAMAGE-INSPECTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:composite-materials:08-damage-inspection, git-history:composite-materials:08-damage-inspection]",
