        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "composite-materials",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[damage, inspection]",
        "section": "composite-materials",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Damage Mechanics and NDT Inspection",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BVID DEFINITION (FAA AC 20-107B):\n   ───────────────────────────────────\n   Damage not found during walk-around / preflight inspection\n   ≤ 0.3 in. (7.6 mm) dent depth → BVID\n   > 0.3 in. and visible from 1.5 m → VID (Visible Impact Damage)\n   Structure must sustain BVID for full design service life\n   Structure must sustain limit load with VID\n```"
    },
